Today's KOSPI -5.54% plunge dealt a direct blow to the semiconductor sector
representing 76.6% of held assets, but with cumulative cost-basis returns of
SK Hynix +169%, Samsung Electronics +96%, and KODEX Semiconductor +86%, this
is "giving back a portion of gains" rather than a loss-realization event.

Two key checkpoints remain:

1) Whether Broadcom-driven AI CapEx slowdown concerns materialize vs.
   remain one-off noise.
   - If realized: entering the late cycle of the semiconductor cycle →
     weight reduction needed
   - If noise: after foreign selling ends and KOSPI 8,000 support is
     confirmed, staged-buy opportunity

2) Resolving SK Hynix 65%-of-holdings single-stock risk.
   - With an average cost of 768,347KRW and current price of 2,070,000KRW,
     unrealized gains are very large; from a tax perspective (ISA non-taxable
     limit), a separate [mode: rebalance] session is needed to review a
     staged profit-taking strategy. No decision in this daily report.

KODEX AI Power Core Infra is the only holding with a negative cost return,
but with 20d -30.5% trend weakness now extended, there is no clear basis for
either a stop-loss or additional buy. Watch mode through the -20% cost-basis
threshold; if reached, recommend immediate re-analysis in a separate single mode.

Today, "not acting" is the best action.
